h(2, id: "tree-sitter") { 18. tree-sitter grammar }

p {
    Editor highlighting for b{.du} files comes from a tree-sitter grammar:
    link("https://github.com/pbarot2009/tree-sitter-docup"){tree-sitter-docup}.
    It parses the same language this compiler accepts, so editors see the same
    blocks and inlines described in sections 4 to 15.
}

p {
    The grammar version tracks the compiler. Grammar code{0.3.2} supports DocUP
    code{0.3.2} (see code{docup version}). Grammar code{MAJOR.MINOR} always
    equals the compiler it supports; grammar code{PATCH} bumps for grammar-only
    fixes.
}

h(3, id: "tree-sitter-covered") { 18.1 What is covered }

p { Every block from section 5 onward: }

list {
    item { code{meta}, code{h}, code{p}, code{codeblock}, code{hr} }
    item { code{list} with code{item} and code{task}, nestable }
    item { code{quote}, nestable }
    item { code{image}, code{table} with code{row} and code{cell} }
    item { code{callout}, code{raw}, code{math}, code{toc} }
    item { code{footnote} with code{fn} references, code{include} }
}

p { Every inline from section 6: }

list {
    item { code{b}, code{i}, code{strike}, code{code}, code{m} }
    item { code{link("url")}, code{fn(id)} }
    item { Prose escapes code{{}, code{\}}, code{\\!}, code{\\} }}
}

p {
    Strings, numbers, booleans, attribute lists, comments, and verbatim
    code{{! ... !}} scopes (with code{\\!}, code{!\}}, and code{\\!} escapes)
    follow sections 3.2, 3.3, and 3.5 exactly.
}

h(3, id: "tree-sitter-parse-vs-sema") { 18.2 Parsing versus checking }

p {
    The grammar parses structure; it does not repeat section 16. A heading
    outside code{h(1)} to code{h(6)}, an unknown callout type, a ragged table,
    or a codeblock with both code{src} and a raw body all parse, and the
    compiler reports them. One document, one reading — the grammar and the
    compiler agree on the tree, and only the compiler judges it.
}

h(3, id: "tree-sitter-helix") { 18.3 Helix setup }

p { Build the grammar library from the grammar repository: }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
cd tree-sitter-docup
tree-sitter build -o ~/.config/helix/runtime/grammars/docup.so .
mkdir -p ~/.config/helix/runtime/queries/docup
cp queries/*.scm ~/.config/helix/runtime/queries/docup/
!}

p { Register the language in code{~/.config/helix/languages.toml}: }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
[[language]]
name = "docup"
scope = "source.docup"
file-types = ["du"]
comment-token = "//"
grammar = "docup"
!}

p {
    Then code{hx --health docup} shows the parser and the highlight queries as
    ready, and code{hx file.du} highlights.
}

h(3, id: "tree-sitter-queries") { 18.4 Queries }

p { The grammar ships five query files: }

table {
    row(header: true) {
        cell { File }
        cell { Used for }
    }
    row {
        cell { code{highlights.scm} }
        cell { Keywords, strings, numbers, links }
    }
    row {
        cell { code{injections.scm} }
        cell { codeblock code{lang} into that language, math into LaTeX }
    }
    row {
        cell { code{folds.scm} }
        cell { Foldable blocks }
    }
    row {
        cell { code{indents.scm} }
        cell { Auto-indent }
    }
    row {
        cell { code{textobjects.scm} }
        cell { Blocks as functions, attributes as parameters }
    }
}
